    "https://werkenbij.vu.nl/vacatures/phd-candidate-epic-project-amsterdam-1350349": {
      "title": "PhD Candidate EPIC Project",
      "description": "PhD Candidate EPIC Project | Werken bij VU Vacatures Faculteit/Dienst Faculteiten Academisch Centrum Tandheelkunde Amsterdam (ACTA) Faculteit der Bètawetenschappen Faculteit der Gedrags- en Bewegingswetenschappen Faculteit der  Sociale en Geesteswetenschappen Faculteit der Geneeskunde Faculteit der Rechtsgeleerdheid School of Business and Economics Diensten Bestuurszaken Communicatie & Marketing Dienst Universitaire Relaties & Fondswerving Facilitaire Campus Organisatie Financiën HRM, Arbo & Milieu Informatietechnologie Student- en Onderwijszaken Universiteitsbibliotheek Jong talent PhD Student-assistent Stage Over ons Over ons VU arbeidsvoorwaarden: uitgebreid en flexibel VU persoonlijk: ontwikkelen, erkennen en waarderen VU identiteit: veilig, verantwoord en inclusief VU Campus: groen, rookvrij en sportief VU sollicitatie: proces, screening en participatie Ik ben een kandidaat Ga naar mijn persoonlijke pagina Log in als medewerker Log in 0 NL EN PhD Candidate EPIC Project Ga terug ACTA Gebouw 1 / 1 PhD Sluit op 16-11-2026 Amsterdam Academisch Centrum Tandheelkunde Amsterdam MSc Publicatiedatum 21-10-2026 Solliciteer direct PhD Candidate EPIC Project ACTA Gebouw Amsterdam 1 / 1 Academisch Centrum Tandheelkunde Amsterdam PhD MSc Sluit op 16-11-2026 Publicatiedatum 21-10-2026 Solliciteer direct Endolysin-Based Therapies Against Implant-Associated Biofilm Infections (EPIC Project) Your function Project overview Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a major healthcare challenge. Prosthetic joint infections, often caused by Staphylococcus aureus and Staphylococcus epidermidis , are difficult to treat because these bacteria form biofilms that protect them from antibiotics and host defenses. Within the NWO-funded EPIC (Endolysin-based Protective Implant nanoCarriers) consortium, ACTA, the University of Twente, Micreos, LipoCoat, and clinical partners are developing innovative endolysin-loaded nanocarriers to prevent and treat implant-associated infections. We seek a highly motivated PhD candidate to investigate the antimicrobial efficacy, anti-biofilm activity, biosafety, and host compatibility of novel endolysin formulations. Your role You will: Investigate the antimicrobial efficacy and biosafety of endolysin-based formulations Evaluate activity against planktonic and biofilm-associated S. aureus and S. epidermidis , including MRSA Develop advanced in vitro biofilm and infection models, including microfluidic systems Assess activity against intracellular staphylococci and monitor resistance development Evaluate cytotoxicity, immune responses, and effects on bone-related cells using human cell culture and 3D tissue models Collaborate with academic and industrial consortium partners Publish findings in peer-reviewed journals and present at scientific conferences You will be based in both the Department of Preventive Dentistry and the Department of Oral Cell Biology at ACTA and work in an interdisciplinary environment spanning microbiology, cell biology, biomaterials, and host-microbe interactions. The supervisory team consists of Prof. dr. Bastiaan Krom, Prof. dr. Astrid Bakker, dr. ing. Michel Hoogenkamp, and dr. Jianfeng Jin. Your profile You have: A Master's degree (or near completion) in Microbiology, Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Biology, Cell Biology, Immunology, Biotechnology, Biochemistry, or a related field Experience with microbiology, biofilm research, mammalian cell culture, molecular biology, and/or microscopy. Strong analytical and communication skills An interest in translational biomedical research and antimicrobial resistance The ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team Excellent English language skills Applicants already eligible to work in the Netherlands are strongly encouraged to apply. Applications requiring immigration sponsorship may not be prioritized due to project timelines and administrative considerations What do we offer? A challenging position in a socially engaged organisation. At ACTA, you contribute to education, research and service for a better world. And that is valuable. So in return for your efforts, we offer you: a salary of minimum € 3.204,00 (PhD) and maximum € 4.051,00 (PhD) gross per month, on a full-time basis. This is based on UFO profile PhD candidate. a 4-year PhD position (initial 1-year contract, extended by 3 years following positive evaluation). We also offer you attractive fringe benefits and regulations. Some examples: A full-time 38-hour working week comes with a holiday leave entitlement of 232 hours per year. 8% holiday allowance and 8.3% end-of-year bonus Solid pension scheme (ABP) Contribution to commuting expenses Group insured for partial disability with employer contribution of 50% of the premium Access to state-of-the-art research facilities Opportunities for collaboration with academic and industry partners Participation in national and international conferences and training activities About us ACTA is the joint Faculty of Dentistry of the University of Amsterdam and Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam and is internationally recognized for its research, education, and patient care in oral health. Interested Are you interested in this position and do you believe that your experience will contribute to the further development of our university? In that case, we encourage you to submit your application. Please submit: Motivation letter Curriculum vitae Contact details of two academic references For questions, contact: dr. ing. Michel Hoogenkamp Department of Preventive Dentistry, ACTA m.hoogenkamp@acta.nl Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. The first round of interviews is expected to take place at the end of November, and the preferred start date for the successful candidate is 1 February 2027. Submitting a diploma is part of the application process. Applications received by e-mail will not be considered. Acquisition in response to this advertisement is not appreciated. Your function Project overview Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a major healthcare challenge. Prosthetic joint infections, often caused by Staphylococcus aureus and Staphylococcus epidermidis , are difficult to treat because these bacteria form biofilms that protect them from antibiotics and host defenses. Within the NWO-funded EPIC (Endolysin-based Protective Implant nanoCarriers) consortium, ACTA, the University of Twente, Micreos, LipoCoat, and clinical partners are developing innovative endolysin-loaded nanocarriers to prevent and treat implant-associated infections. We seek a highly motivated PhD candidate to investigate the antimicrobial efficacy, anti-biofilm activity, biosafety, and host compatibility of novel endolysin formulations. Your role You will: Investigate the antimicrobial efficacy and biosafety of endolysin-based formulations Evaluate activity against planktonic and biofilm-associated S. aureus and S. epidermidis , including MRSA Develop advanced in vitro biofilm and infection models, including microfluidic systems Assess activity against intracellular staphylococci and monitor resistance development Evaluate cytotoxicity, immune responses, and effects on bone-related cells using human cell culture and 3D tissue models Collaborate with academic and industrial consortium partners Publish findings in peer-reviewed journals and present at scientific conferences You will be based in both the Department of Preventive Dentistry and the Department of Oral Cell Biology at ACTA and work in an interdisciplinary environment spanning microbiology, cell biology, biomaterials, and host-microbe interactions. The supervisory team consists of Prof. dr. Bastiaan Krom, Prof. dr. Astrid Bakker, dr. ing. Michel Hoogenkamp, and dr. Jianfeng Jin. Your profile You have: A Master's degree (or near completion) in Microbiology, Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Biology, Cell Biology, Immunology, Biotechnology, Biochemistry, or a related field Experience with microbiology, biofilm research, mammalian cell culture, molecular biology, and/or microscopy. Strong analytical and communication skills An interest in translational biomedical research and antimicrobial resistance The ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team Excellent English language skills Applicants already eligible to work in the Netherlands are strongly encouraged to apply. Applications requiring immigration sponsorship may not be prioritized due to project timelines and administrative considerations What do we offer? A challenging position in a socially engaged organisation. At ACTA, you contribute to education, research and service for a better world. And that is valuable. So in return for your efforts, we offer you: a salary of minimum € 3.204,00 (PhD) and maximum € 4.051,00 (PhD) gross per month, on a full-time basis. This is based on UFO profile PhD candidate. a 4-year PhD position (initial 1-year contract, extended by 3 years following positive evaluation). We also offer you attractive fringe benefits and regulations. Some examples: A full-time 38-hour working week comes with a holiday leave entitlement of 232 hours per year. 8% holiday allowance and 8.3% end-of-year bonus Solid pension scheme (ABP) Contribution to commuting expenses Group insured for partial disability with employer contribution of 50% of the premium Access to state-of-the-art research facilities Opportunities for collaboration with academic and industry partners Participation in national and international conferences and training activities About us ACTA is the joint Faculty of Dentistry of the University of Amsterdam and Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam and is internationally recognized for its research, education, and patient care in oral health. Vragen over de vacature? Neem contact op met Michel Hoogenkamp Assistant Professor Stuur een e-mail Interested Are you interested in this position and do you believe that your experience will contribute to the further development of our university? In that case, we encourage you to submit your application. Please submit: Motivation letter Curriculum vitae Contact details of two academic references For questions, contact: dr. ing. Michel Hoogenkamp Department of Preventive Dentistry, ACTA m.hoogenkamp@acta.nl Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. The first round of interviews is expected to take place at the end of November, and the preferred start date for the successful candidate is 1 February 2027. Submitting a diploma is part of the application process. Applications received by e-mail will not be considered. Acquisition in response to this advertisement is not appreciated. Vragen over de vacature? Neem contact op met Michel Hoogenkamp Assistant Professor Stuur een e-mail Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1 Sollicitatie ontvangen Wij hebben je sollicitatie goed ontvangen. We streven ernaar om je zo snel mogelijk een eerste reactie te geven. Normaal gesproken is dat twee weken na het verstrijken van de deadline. Stap 2 Screening CV Een selectiecommissie beoordeelt of je voldoet aan de gestelde wensen/eisen voor de vacature. Bij een positieve beoordeling nodigen we je uit voor een eerste (hybride) sollicitatiegesprek. Stap 3 1e Gesprek Sollicitatiegesprekken vinden veelal plaats op een VU- locatie, maar soms word je eerst uitgenodigd voor een videogesprek. De VU maakt hiervoor gebruik van MS teams. Stap 4 2e Gesprek Voor het tweede gesprek vragen we je meestal om naar onze VU campus te komen. Stap 5 Pre-employment screening Het overleggen van een diploma wordt altijd gevraagd bij indiensttreding. Afhankelijk van de functie kan een assessment onderdeel uitmaken van de sollicitatieprocedure. Stap 6 Optioneel antecedentenonderzoek Afhankelijk van de functie en het bijbehorende risicoprofiel, kan een antecedentenonderzoek door de VU worden uitgevoerd. Daarbij kan worden gevraagd om referenties en/of een Verklaring omtrent Gedrag (VOG) aan te leveren. In het kader van kennisveiligheid kunnen wij ook publieke beschikbare social media accounts en publieke uitlatingen van jou op internet bekijken. Stap 7 In dienst Welkom je bent in dienst bij de Vrije Universiteit!! Andere interessante vacatures PhD in experimental physics: how do you make the first antimatter molecule? 0.8 / 1 Faculty of Science PhD MSc Closes on 28-02-2027 Publicatiedatum 23-10-2026 0.4 km Help make the first measurement of how a proton and a hydrogen atom bind into a molecule. With extreme-UV lasers and ion traps, you will study the most fundamental atomic collisions and find out how the first antimatter molecules could be made. Bekijk vacature PhD Position in Space Law and Artificial Intelligence 0.8 / 1 Faculty of Law PhD LL.M Closes on 27-11-2026 Publicatiedatum 07-10-2026 0.4 km Who sets the rules when AI turns Earth Observation data into decisions about security, resilience and society? Join us as a PhD researcher and help shape the unique intersection of space law and artificial intelligence. Bekijk vacature PhD Position in Formal Methods for Concurrent Cryptographic Protocols 1 / 1 Faculty of Science PhD MSc Closes on 30-10-2026 Publicatiedatum 11-06-2026 0.4 km The goal of this project is to use formal methods to develop a systematic way to describe concurrent cryptographic protocols and to reason about their security. If this sounds interesting to you, please apply at Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam (VU). Bekijk vacature PhD Position in Neuroimaging, LLM, Genetics and Cross-species comparison 1 / 1 Faculty of Science PhD MSc Closes on 15-12-2026 Publicatiedatum 26-10-2026 0.5 km How does the organization of the human brain vary across species, and how has this diversity emerged over the course of evolution? Bekijk vacature PhD-student in cellular neuroscience 1 / 1 Faculty of Science PhD MSc Closes on 06-11-2026 Publicatiedatum 19-10-2026 0.5 km Decipher how mRNA localization and local protein synthesis regulate synapse formation and function. Bekijk vacature PhD - Physics of Human-Made Molecular Machines 1 / 1 Faculty of Science PhD MSc Closes on 31-10-2026 Publicatiedatum 12-10-2026 0.5 km How can synthetic nanomotors generate force and work together in molecular machines? Can we design single-motor experiments to quantify their performance on dedicated tasks? Join our world-class consortium and pioneer human-made molecular machines! Bekijk vacature Mis jouw droombaan niet! Stel job alert in Privacy Cookies Disclaimer VU.nl Deze website maakt gebruik van cookies Wij, en derde partijen, maken op onze website gebruik van cookies. Wij gebruiken cookies om ervoor te zorgen dat onze website goed functioneert, om jouw voorkeuren op te slaan, om inzicht te verkrijgen in bezoekersgedrag, maar ook voor marketing en social media doeleinden (laten zien van gepersonaliseerde advertenties). Door op ‘Accepteren’ te klikken, ga je akkoord met het gebruik van alle cookies. In onze Cookieverklaring kun je meer lezen over de cookies die wij gebruiken en kun je jouw voorkeuren opslaan of wijzigen.  Door ‘Weigeren’ te klikken ga je alleen akkoord met het gebruik van functionele cookies. Functioneel Functionele cookies zorgen ervoor dat deze website informatie kan onthouden die van invloed is op het gedrag en de vormgeving van de website, zoals bijvoorbeeld welke vacatures jouw favorieten zijn. Statistieken Statistische cookies helpen ons te begrijpen hoe bezoekers deze website gebruiken, door anoniem gegevens te verzamelen en te rapporteren. Marketing Marketing cookies worden op deze site gebruikt om eventueel video’s via YouTube af te kunnen spelen. Verder ook om relevante advertenties weer te geven tijdens het bezoeken van andere websites. Zelf instellen Weigeren Accepteer geselecteerde cookies Accepteren Lees meer in de cookieverklaring"
