      "title": "Project Manager",
      "description": "Project Manager | Werken bij VU Vacatures Faculteit/Dienst Faculteiten Academisch Centrum Tandheelkunde Amsterdam (ACTA) Faculteit der Bètawetenschappen Faculteit der Gedrags- en Bewegingswetenschappen Faculteit der  Sociale en Geesteswetenschappen Faculteit der Geneeskunde Faculteit der Rechtsgeleerdheid School of Business and Economics Diensten Bestuurszaken Communicatie & Marketing Dienst Universitaire Relaties & Fondswerving Facilitaire Campus Organisatie Financiën HRM, Arbo & Milieu Informatietechnologie Student- en Onderwijszaken Universiteitsbibliotheek Jong talent PhD Student-assistent Stage Over ons Over ons VU arbeidsvoorwaarden: uitgebreid en flexibel VU persoonlijk: ontwikkelen, erkennen en waarderen VU identiteit: veilig, verantwoord en inclusief VU Campus: groen, rookvrij en sportief VU sollicitatie: proces, screening en participatie Ik ben een kandidaat Ga naar mijn persoonlijke pagina Log in als medewerker Log in 0 NL EN Project Manager Ga terug VU Hoofdgebouw 0.9 / 1 Development & Innovation Sluit op 12-11-2026 Amsterdam Institutional Affairs MSc Publicatiedatum 29-10-2026 Solliciteer direct Project Manager VU Hoofdgebouw Amsterdam 0.9 / 1 Institutional Affairs Development & Innovation MSc Sluit op 12-11-2026 Publicatiedatum 29-10-2026 Solliciteer direct Help build VU's new Project Management Pool and steer some of its largest EU-funded research consortia. Do you thrive on structure and getting big research projects across the finish line? We'd love to hear from you. Your function At IXA-GO, we support researchers throughout the full lifecycle of their research — from securing funding to translating results into value for the market and society. IXA-GO brings together grant advisors, programme managers, business and impact developers, and other support professionals. The Grants Office helps scientific staff apply for and manage European and Dutch research grants. To further professionalise our support for large, primarily EU-funded consortium projects, we are setting up a central Project Management Pool to support researchers and faculties with the project management of large European and national consortium projects. Most projects we manage have a consortium size of 7–12 partners and a total budget of €3.5M–€8M. As Project Manager, you provide operational and administrative support to PIs, ensuring smooth delivery of complex, multi-partner projects. You join the Project Management Pool, working both independently and within a matrix team of project managers, programme managers, grants advisors, and project controllers, in close collaboration with the Pool's Coordinating Project Manager. You work closely with coordinating PIs, who hold overall project responsibility. Your key task is to ensure projects deliver results and that risks are caught early. Funding sources vary — from national programmes like NWO Gravitation, KIC, and NWA-ORC to Horizon Europe instruments — each with its own rules. You maintain regular contact with funders' Project Officers to ensure accurate progress reporting and alignment on any project changes. Specific responsibilities: manage administrative processes across multiple projects, ensuring timely reporting and compliance support PIs by leading operational, administrative, financial, and managerial coordination — freeing them to focus on the science liaise with consortium partners and funders' Project Officers on progress reporting provide logistical and administrative support for project and consortium meetings mitigate project risks for VU by monitoring implementation against funding and consortium agreements maximise use of the project budget, working closely with Project Control, Business Control, and department managers coordinate support from other domains — Legal, Finance, HR, Ethics, Business Development. You're the spider in the web Your profile academic mindset, ideally from a research-intensive background, with a working knowledge of project management methods (planning, monitoring, communication, coaching) strong, coaching-style communicator with a track record of supporting and motivating research professionals skilled at coordinating multidisciplinary academic consortia and internal support functions (Legal, Finance, HR, Ethics, Business Development) across departments, faculties, and international partners knowledge of Dutch and European research grants, e.g. Horizon Europe pillar 2, NWA-ORC, NWO KIC independent, proactive, and adaptable, with the organisational sensitivity to balance researchers' needs with funder requirements strong administrative skills — prioritising multiple deadlines and stakeholders, with accurate documentation and adherence to regulations knowledge of financial management in academic settings: budgeting, grant compliance, reporting, and audits excellent English and Dutch, comfortable in a digital working environment, and willing to travel for project meetings PM certification (PRINCE2, PMP) or research management training is a plus What do we offer? An exciting position within an international yet personal university. You are right in the middle of the students, on a green campus within walking distance of the Station Zuid(as). We also offer you: a 12-month contract, with the possibility of extension (up to 48 months), depending on funding (in accordance with art. 2.3 sub 7a CAO NU). a position as research project manager based on the university ranking system (UFO) of  Knowledge Valorisation Officer 4 for a minimum of 0,9 fte a salary of minimum € 3.706 (Scale 10) and maximum €  5.760 (Scale 10) gross per month, on a full-time basis. The exact salary depends on your education and experience a maximum of 29 days of annual leave based on full-time employment (38 hours per week) possibility of choosing an option from the Flexible Working Hours Scheme , which allows you 41 days of leave for a 40-hour work week 8% holiday allowance and 8.3% end-of-year bonus space for personal development, including through membership to professional associations such as ARMA-NL and EARMA About us Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam stands for values-driven education and research. We are open-minded experts with the ability to think freely - a broader mind. Maintaining an entrepreneurial perspective and concentrating on diversity, significance and humanity, we work on sustainable solutions with social impact. By joining forces, across the boundaries of disciplines, we work towards a better world for people and planet. Together we create a safe and respectful working and study climate, and an inspiring environment for education and research. Learn more about our codes of conduct We are located on one physical campus, in the heart of Amsterdam's Zuidas business district, with excellent location and accessibility.  Over 6,150 staff work at the VU and over 31,000 students attend academic education. Diversity Diversity is the driving force of VU Amsterdam. VU wants to be accessible and receptive to diversity in disciplines, cultures, ideas, nationalities, beliefs, preferences and worldviews. We believe that trust, respect, interest and differences lead to new insights and innovation, to sharpness and clarity, to excellence and a broader understanding. We stand for an inclusive community and believe that diversity and internationalisation contribute to the quality of education, research and our services. Therefore, we are always searching for people whose backgrounds and experience contribute to the diversity of the VU community. Interested Apply via the application button before 12 November 2026 , submitting your CV and motivation letter . A first round interview will be scheduled for late November . Start date: As soon as possible. Note: Applications sent by email will not be considered. Sales enquiries in response to this advertisement are not welcome. Your function At IXA-GO, we support researchers throughout the full lifecycle of their research — from securing funding to translating results into value for the market and society. IXA-GO brings together grant advisors, programme managers, business and impact developers, and other support professionals. The Grants Office helps scientific staff apply for and manage European and Dutch research grants. To further professionalise our support for large, primarily EU-funded consortium projects, we are setting up a central Project Management Pool to support researchers and faculties with the project management of large European and national consortium projects. Most projects we manage have a consortium size of 7–12 partners and a total budget of €3.5M–€8M. As Project Manager, you provide operational and administrative support to PIs, ensuring smooth delivery of complex, multi-partner projects. You join the Project Management Pool, working both independently and within a matrix team of project managers, programme managers, grants advisors, and project controllers, in close collaboration with the Pool's Coordinating Project Manager. You work closely with coordinating PIs, who hold overall project responsibility. Your key task is to ensure projects deliver results and that risks are caught early. Funding sources vary — from national programmes like NWO Gravitation, KIC, and NWA-ORC to Horizon Europe instruments — each with its own rules. You maintain regular contact with funders' Project Officers to ensure accurate progress reporting and alignment on any project changes. Specific responsibilities: manage administrative processes across multiple projects, ensuring timely reporting and compliance support PIs by leading operational, administrative, financial, and managerial coordination — freeing them to focus on the science liaise with consortium partners and funders' Project Officers on progress reporting provide logistical and administrative support for project and consortium meetings mitigate project risks for VU by monitoring implementation against funding and consortium agreements maximise use of the project budget, working closely with Project Control, Business Control, and department managers coordinate support from other domains — Legal, Finance, HR, Ethics, Business Development. You're the spider in the web Your profile academic mindset, ideally from a research-intensive background, with a working knowledge of project management methods (planning, monitoring, communication, coaching) strong, coaching-style communicator with a track record of supporting and motivating research professionals skilled at coordinating multidisciplinary academic consortia and internal support functions (Legal, Finance, HR, Ethics, Business Development) across departments, faculties, and international partners knowledge of Dutch and European research grants, e.g. Horizon Europe pillar 2, NWA-ORC, NWO KIC independent, proactive, and adaptable, with the organisational sensitivity to balance researchers' needs with funder requirements strong administrative skills — prioritising multiple deadlines and stakeholders, with accurate documentation and adherence to regulations knowledge of financial management in academic settings: budgeting, grant compliance, reporting, and audits excellent English and Dutch, comfortable in a digital working environment, and willing to travel for project meetings PM certification (PRINCE2, PMP) or research management training is a plus What do we offer? An exciting position within an international yet personal university. You are right in the middle of the students, on a green campus within walking distance of the Station Zuid(as). We also offer you: a 12-month contract, with the possibility of extension (up to 48 months), depending on funding (in accordance with art. 2.3 sub 7a CAO NU). a position as research project manager based on the university ranking system (UFO) of  Knowledge Valorisation Officer 4 for a minimum of 0,9 fte a salary of minimum € 3.706 (Scale 10) and maximum €  5.760 (Scale 10) gross per month, on a full-time basis. The exact salary depends on your education and experience a maximum of 29 days of annual leave based on full-time employment (38 hours per week) possibility of choosing an option from the Flexible Working Hours Scheme , which allows you 41 days of leave for a 40-hour work week 8% holiday allowance and 8.3% end-of-year bonus space for personal development, including through membership to professional associations such as ARMA-NL and EARMA About us Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam stands for values-driven education and research. We are open-minded experts with the ability to think freely - a broader mind. Maintaining an entrepreneurial perspective and concentrating on diversity, significance and humanity, we work on sustainable solutions with social impact. By joining forces, across the boundaries of disciplines, we work towards a better world for people and planet. Together we create a safe and respectful working and study climate, and an inspiring environment for education and research. Learn more about our codes of conduct We are located on one physical campus, in the heart of Amsterdam's Zuidas business district, with excellent location and accessibility.  Over 6,150 staff work at the VU and over 31,000 students attend academic education. Diversity Diversity is the driving force of VU Amsterdam. VU wants to be accessible and receptive to diversity in disciplines, cultures, ideas, nationalities, beliefs, preferences and worldviews. We believe that trust, respect, interest and differences lead to new insights and innovation, to sharpness and clarity, to excellence and a broader understanding. We stand for an inclusive community and believe that diversity and internationalisation contribute to the quality of education, research and our services. Therefore, we are always searching for people whose backgrounds and experience contribute to the diversity of the VU community. Vragen over de vacature? Neem contact op met Margreth Lieftink Management Assistant IXA-GO +31 (0)6 81387910 Stuur een e-mail Interested Apply via the application button before 12 November 2026 , submitting your CV and motivation letter . A first round interview will be scheduled for late November . Start date: As soon as possible. Note: Applications sent by email will not be considered. Sales enquiries in response to this advertisement are not welcome. Vragen over de vacature? Neem contact op met Margreth Lieftink Management Assistant IXA-GO +31 (0)6 81387910 Stuur een e-mail Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1 Sollicitatie ontvangen Wij hebben je sollicitatie goed ontvangen. We streven ernaar om je zo snel mogelijk een eerste reactie te geven. Normaal gesproken is dat twee weken na het verstrijken van de deadline. Stap 2 Screening CV Een selectiecommissie beoordeelt of je voldoet aan de gestelde wensen/eisen voor de vacature. Bij een positieve beoordeling nodigen we je uit voor een eerste (hybride) sollicitatiegesprek. Stap 3 1e Gesprek Sollicitatiegesprekken vinden veelal plaats op een VU- locatie, maar soms word je eerst uitgenodigd voor een videogesprek. De VU maakt hiervoor gebruik van MS teams. Stap 4 2e Gesprek Voor het tweede gesprek vragen we je meestal om naar onze VU campus te komen. Stap 5 Pre-employment screening Het overleggen van een diploma wordt altijd gevraagd bij indiensttreding. Afhankelijk van de functie kan een assessment onderdeel uitmaken van de sollicitatieprocedure. Stap 6 Optioneel antecedentenonderzoek Afhankelijk van de functie en het bijbehorende risicoprofiel, kan een antecedentenonderzoek door de VU worden uitgevoerd. Daarbij kan worden gevraagd om referenties en/of een Verklaring omtrent Gedrag (VOG) aan te leveren. In het kader van kennisveiligheid kunnen wij ook publieke beschikbare social media accounts en publieke uitlatingen van jou op internet bekijken. Stap 7 In dienst Welkom je bent in dienst bij de Vrije Universiteit!! Andere interessante vacatures Er zijn geen andere relevante vacatures beschikbaar schrijf je snel in voor onze job alert. Mis jouw droombaan niet! Stel job alert in Privacy Cookies Disclaimer VU.nl Deze website maakt gebruik van cookies Wij, en derde partijen, maken op onze website gebruik van cookies. Wij gebruiken cookies om ervoor te zorgen dat onze website goed functioneert, om jouw voorkeuren op te slaan, om inzicht te verkrijgen in bezoekersgedrag, maar ook voor marketing en social media doeleinden (laten zien van gepersonaliseerde advertenties). Door op ‘Accepteren’ te klikken, ga je akkoord met het gebruik van alle cookies. In onze Cookieverklaring kun je meer lezen over de cookies die wij gebruiken en kun je jouw voorkeuren opslaan of wijzigen.  Door ‘Weigeren’ te klikken ga je alleen akkoord met het gebruik van functionele cookies. Functioneel Functionele cookies zorgen ervoor dat deze website informatie kan onthouden die van invloed is op het gedrag en de vormgeving van de website, zoals bijvoorbeeld welke vacatures jouw favorieten zijn. Statistieken Statistische cookies helpen ons te begrijpen hoe bezoekers deze website gebruiken, door anoniem gegevens te verzamelen en te rapporteren. Marketing Marketing cookies worden op deze site gebruikt om eventueel video’s via YouTube af te kunnen spelen. Verder ook om relevante advertenties weer te geven tijdens het bezoeken van andere websites. Zelf instellen Weigeren Accepteer geselecteerde cookies Accepteren Lees meer in de cookieverklaring"
