    "https://werkenbij.vu.nl/vacatures/postdoc-executive-lawmaking-in-eu-migration-law-amsterdam-1357203": {
      "title": "Postdoc: Executive lawmaking in EU migration law",
      "description": "Postdoc: Executive lawmaking in EU migration law | Werken bij VU Vacatures Faculteit/Dienst Faculteiten Academisch Centrum Tandheelkunde Amsterdam (ACTA) Faculteit der Bètawetenschappen Faculteit der Gedrags- en Bewegingswetenschappen Faculteit der  Sociale en Geesteswetenschappen Faculteit der Geneeskunde Faculteit der Rechtsgeleerdheid School of Business and Economics Diensten Bestuurszaken Communicatie & Marketing Dienst Universitaire Relaties & Fondswerving Facilitaire Campus Organisatie Financiën HRM, Arbo & Milieu Informatietechnologie Student- en Onderwijszaken Universiteitsbibliotheek Jong talent PhD Student-assistent Stage Over ons Over ons VU arbeidsvoorwaarden: uitgebreid en flexibel VU persoonlijk: ontwikkelen, erkennen en waarderen VU identiteit: veilig, verantwoord en inclusief VU Campus: groen, rookvrij en sportief VU sollicitatie: proces, screening en participatie Ik ben een kandidaat Ga naar mijn persoonlijke pagina Log in als medewerker Log in 0 NL EN Postdoc: Executive lawmaking in EU migration law Ga terug Initium Gebouw 0.8 / 1 Researcher / Postdoc Sluit op 08-12-2026 Amsterdam Faculty of Law Postdoc Publicatiedatum 13-11-2026 Solliciteer direct Postdoc: Executive lawmaking in EU migration law Initium Gebouw Amsterdam 0.8 / 1 Faculty of Law Researcher / Postdoc Postdoc Sluit op 08-12-2026 Publicatiedatum 13-11-2026 Solliciteer direct Are you interested in the delegation of legislative power in EU migration law? Would you like to conduct research into EU legislation, help coordinate a research project, and contribute to its impact? Please apply to this vacancy at the ACMRL. Your function In EU law, legislative power is often delegated to the European Commission. In the field of migration law, this possibility has increased with the adoption of the European Pact on Migration and Asylum in 2024. This vacancy is part of a VIDI project funded by the Dutch National Research Council (NWO) entitled 'Executive supremacy? Executive lawmaking in migration law'. This project aims to map the scope of executive legislation in migration law in Europe and to critically interrogate its normative legitimacy. The postdoc in this project conducts research into lawmaking by the European Commission in the field of migration and asylum law. This research is both empirical (what is the scope) and normative (is it sufficiently constrained to minimize the potential for arbitrary power). In addition, the postdoc will participate in the coordination and management of the project as well as in the organization of societal and scientific impact activities. The appointment will initially be for one year. After satisfactory evaluation of the initial appointment, it will be extended by two years to a total duration of three years. Your duties conducting research into lawmaking by the European Commission in the field of migration and asylum law; presenting results at conferences, in blogposts and in a policy brief; publishing results in scientific journals and/or books; organizing seminars, public meetings and a final conference of the VIDI project; teaching in ACMRL’s bachelor’s and/or master’s courses (max 15% of appointment) Your profile you have a PhD in law, or your PhD manuscript is approved by the reading/assessment committee; you have expertise in EU constitutional law and/or migration law; you have strong verbal and writing skills in English, and preferably also in Dutch; you can work independently and collaboratively; you have strong planning and organizational skills As a university, we strive for equal opportunities for all, recognising that diversity takes many forms. We believe that diversity in all its complexity is invaluable for the quality of our teaching, research and service. We are always looking for talent with diverse backgrounds and experiences. This also means that we are committed to creating an inclusive community so that we can use diversity as an asset. We realise that each individual brings a unique set of skills, expertise and mindset. Therefore we are happy to invite anyone who recognises themselves in the profile to apply, even if you do not meet all the requirements. What do we offer? A challenging position in a socially engaged organisation. At VU Amsterdam, you contribute to education, research and service for a better world. And that is valuable. So in return for your efforts, we offer you: a salary of minimum € 3.706,00 (Scale 10) and maximum € 5.760,00 (Scale 10) gross per month, on a full-time basis. This is based on UFO profile Researcher 4. The exact salary depends on your education and experience. a position for at least 0.8 FTE. Your employment contract will initially last 1 year. After satisfactory evaluation of the initial appointment, it will be extended by two years to a total duration of three years. We also offer you attractive fringe benefits and regulations. Some examples: A full-time 38-hour working week comes with a holiday leave entitlement of 232 hours per year. If you choose to work 40 hours, you have 96 extra holiday leave hours on an annual basis. For part-timers, this is calculated pro rata. 8% holiday allowance and 8.3% end-of-year bonus contribution to commuting expenses space for personal development discount on (and occasionally exclusive access to) theater performances and courses at the Griffioen Cultural Center About us Amsterdam Centre for Migration and Refugee Law (ACMRL) The Amsterdam Centre for Migration and Refugee Law (ACMRL) at VU Amsterdam is one of the world's largest research centres in the field migration and refugee law. It conducts research on topics such as asylum law and family migration, actively contributes to public debate and government advisory committees, and publishes accessible legal insights on topical issues of migration law on Verblijfblog.nl . The Centre also offers an international master’s track (LL.M) on International Migration and Refugee Law , runs a Migration Law Clinic that provides expert legal advice, and provides postgraduate courses for practising lawyers. Faculty of Law At the Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam’s Faculty of Law we train lawyers and criminologists to develop sharp critical minds, with a strong focus on the societal relevance of law. We offer Bachelor’s programmes in four main fields: Law, Notarial Law, Law in Society and Criminology. In addition, we offer an extensive range of Master’s programmes as well as contract education (for non-student visitors). Much of our research is both international and multidisciplinary in character. Our teaching and research embody the values of cooperation and diversity. We encourage each other to view problems from different perspectives, to think critically, develop a broader mind and arrive at creative legal solutions together. Are you interested in joining the Faculty of Law? You will work in an active and inspiring academic environment. Together with your colleagues, you will contribute to the excellence of teaching and research in a pleasant and collegial working environment. You will join over 400 staff members responsible for a student body of 4,500. Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam stands for values-driven education and research. We are open-minded experts with the ability to think freely - a broader mind. Maintaining an entrepreneurial perspective and concentrating on diversity, significance and humanity, we work on sustainable solutions with social impact. By joining forces, across the boundaries of disciplines, we work towards a better world for people and planet. Together we create a safe and respectful working and study climate, and an inspiring environment for education and research. Learn more about our codes of conduct We are located on one physical campus, in the heart of Amsterdam's Zuidas business district, with excellent location and accessibility. Over 6,150 staff work at the VU and over 31,000 students attend academic education. Diversity Diversity is the driving force of VU Amsterdam. VU wants to be accessible and receptive to diversity in disciplines, cultures, ideas, nationalities, beliefs, preferences and worldviews. We believe that trust, respect, interest and differences lead to new insights and innovation, to sharpness and clarity, to excellence and a broader understanding. We stand for an inclusive community and believe that diversity and internationalisation contribute to the quality of education, research and our services. Therefore, we are always searching for people whose backgrounds and experience contribute to the diversity of the VU community. Interested Are you interested in this position? We invite you to apply by submitting the following documents: motivation letter (cover letter); curriculum vitae (CV); a brief reflection on and outline for the research to be conducted (max. 1 A4) Motivation letters and research outlines generated with AI language tools will not be considered. Submitting a diploma and a reference check are part of the application process. The (first round of) interviews will be held on 17/18 December 2026. The start date is 1 April 2027 at the latest. Applications received by e-mail will not be considered. Acquisition in response to this advertisement is not appreciated. Your function In EU law, legislative power is often delegated to the European Commission. In the field of migration law, this possibility has increased with the adoption of the European Pact on Migration and Asylum in 2024. This vacancy is part of a VIDI project funded by the Dutch National Research Council (NWO) entitled 'Executive supremacy? Executive lawmaking in migration law'. This project aims to map the scope of executive legislation in migration law in Europe and to critically interrogate its normative legitimacy. The postdoc in this project conducts research into lawmaking by the European Commission in the field of migration and asylum law. This research is both empirical (what is the scope) and normative (is it sufficiently constrained to minimize the potential for arbitrary power). In addition, the postdoc will participate in the coordination and management of the project as well as in the organization of societal and scientific impact activities. The appointment will initially be for one year. After satisfactory evaluation of the initial appointment, it will be extended by two years to a total duration of three years. Your duties conducting research into lawmaking by the European Commission in the field of migration and asylum law; presenting results at conferences, in blogposts and in a policy brief; publishing results in scientific journals and/or books; organizing seminars, public meetings and a final conference of the VIDI project; teaching in ACMRL’s bachelor’s and/or master’s courses (max 15% of appointment) Your profile you have a PhD in law, or your PhD manuscript is approved by the reading/assessment committee; you have expertise in EU constitutional law and/or migration law; you have strong verbal and writing skills in English, and preferably also in Dutch; you can work independently and collaboratively; you have strong planning and organizational skills As a university, we strive for equal opportunities for all, recognising that diversity takes many forms. We believe that diversity in all its complexity is invaluable for the quality of our teaching, research and service. We are always looking for talent with diverse backgrounds and experiences. This also means that we are committed to creating an inclusive community so that we can use diversity as an asset. We realise that each individual brings a unique set of skills, expertise and mindset. Therefore we are happy to invite anyone who recognises themselves in the profile to apply, even if you do not meet all the requirements. What do we offer? A challenging position in a socially engaged organisation. At VU Amsterdam, you contribute to education, research and service for a better world. And that is valuable. So in return for your efforts, we offer you: a salary of minimum € 3.706,00 (Scale 10) and maximum € 5.760,00 (Scale 10) gross per month, on a full-time basis. This is based on UFO profile Researcher 4. The exact salary depends on your education and experience. a position for at least 0.8 FTE. Your employment contract will initially last 1 year. After satisfactory evaluation of the initial appointment, it will be extended by two years to a total duration of three years. We also offer you attractive fringe benefits and regulations. Some examples: A full-time 38-hour working week comes with a holiday leave entitlement of 232 hours per year. If you choose to work 40 hours, you have 96 extra holiday leave hours on an annual basis. For part-timers, this is calculated pro rata. 8% holiday allowance and 8.3% end-of-year bonus contribution to commuting expenses space for personal development discount on (and occasionally exclusive access to) theater performances and courses at the Griffioen Cultural Center About us Amsterdam Centre for Migration and Refugee Law (ACMRL) The Amsterdam Centre for Migration and Refugee Law (ACMRL) at VU Amsterdam is one of the world's largest research centres in the field migration and refugee law. It conducts research on topics such as asylum law and family migration, actively contributes to public debate and government advisory committees, and publishes accessible legal insights on topical issues of migration law on Verblijfblog.nl . The Centre also offers an international master’s track (LL.M) on International Migration and Refugee Law , runs a Migration Law Clinic that provides expert legal advice, and provides postgraduate courses for practising lawyers. Faculty of Law At the Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam’s Faculty of Law we train lawyers and criminologists to develop sharp critical minds, with a strong focus on the societal relevance of law. We offer Bachelor’s programmes in four main fields: Law, Notarial Law, Law in Society and Criminology. In addition, we offer an extensive range of Master’s programmes as well as contract education (for non-student visitors). Much of our research is both international and multidisciplinary in character. Our teaching and research embody the values of cooperation and diversity. We encourage each other to view problems from different perspectives, to think critically, develop a broader mind and arrive at creative legal solutions together. Are you interested in joining the Faculty of Law? You will work in an active and inspiring academic environment. Together with your colleagues, you will contribute to the excellence of teaching and research in a pleasant and collegial working environment. You will join over 400 staff members responsible for a student body of 4,500. Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam stands for values-driven education and research. We are open-minded experts with the ability to think freely - a broader mind. Maintaining an entrepreneurial perspective and concentrating on diversity, significance and humanity, we work on sustainable solutions with social impact. By joining forces, across the boundaries of disciplines, we work towards a better world for people and planet. Together we create a safe and respectful working and study climate, and an inspiring environment for education and research. Learn more about our codes of conduct We are located on one physical campus, in the heart of Amsterdam's Zuidas business district, with excellent location and accessibility. Over 6,150 staff work at the VU and over 31,000 students attend academic education. Diversity Diversity is the driving force of VU Amsterdam. VU wants to be accessible and receptive to diversity in disciplines, cultures, ideas, nationalities, beliefs, preferences and worldviews. We believe that trust, respect, interest and differences lead to new insights and innovation, to sharpness and clarity, to excellence and a broader understanding. We stand for an inclusive community and believe that diversity and internationalisation contribute to the quality of education, research and our services. Therefore, we are always searching for people whose backgrounds and experience contribute to the diversity of the VU community. Vragen over de vacature? Neem contact op met Lieneke Slingenberg Professor of Migrants and the Rule of Law +31 20 598 6342 Stuur een e-mail Interested Are you interested in this position? We invite you to apply by submitting the following documents: motivation letter (cover letter); curriculum vitae (CV); a brief reflection on and outline for the research to be conducted (max. 1 A4) Motivation letters and research outlines generated with AI language tools will not be considered. Submitting a diploma and a reference check are part of the application process. The (first round of) interviews will be held on 17/18 December 2026. The start date is 1 April 2027 at the latest. Applications received by e-mail will not be considered. Acquisition in response to this advertisement is not appreciated. Vragen over de vacature? Neem contact op met Lieneke Slingenberg Professor of Migrants and the Rule of Law +31 20 598 6342 Stuur een e-mail Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1 Sollicitatie ontvangen Wij hebben je sollicitatie goed ontvangen. We streven ernaar om je zo snel mogelijk een eerste reactie te geven. Normaal gesproken is dat twee weken na het verstrijken van de deadline. Stap 2 Screening CV Een selectiecommissie beoordeelt of je voldoet aan de gestelde wensen/eisen voor de vacature. Bij een positieve beoordeling nodigen we je uit voor een eerste (hybride) sollicitatiegesprek. Stap 3 1e Gesprek Sollicitatiegesprekken vinden veelal plaats op een VU- locatie, maar soms word je eerst uitgenodigd voor een videogesprek. De VU maakt hiervoor gebruik van MS teams. Stap 4 2e Gesprek Voor het tweede gesprek vragen we je meestal om naar onze VU campus te komen. Stap 5 Pre-employment screening Het overleggen van een diploma wordt altijd gevraagd bij indiensttreding. Afhankelijk van de functie kan een assessment onderdeel uitmaken van de sollicitatieprocedure. Stap 6 Optioneel antecedentenonderzoek Afhankelijk van de functie en het bijbehorende risicoprofiel, kan een antecedentenonderzoek door de VU worden uitgevoerd. Daarbij kan worden gevraagd om referenties en/of een Verklaring omtrent Gedrag (VOG) aan te leveren. In het kader van kennisveiligheid kunnen wij ook publieke beschikbare social media accounts en publieke uitlatingen van jou op internet bekijken. Stap 7 In dienst Welkom je bent in dienst bij de Vrije Universiteit!! Andere interessante vacatures Postdoctoral Researcher Land-Use and Grid Modelling for Biodiversity Restoration 0.8 / 1 Faculty of Science Researcher / Postdoc Postdoc Sluit op 03-12-2026 Publicatiedatum 12-11-2026 0.0 km How can Europe's electricity networks support biodiversity restoration? Join our research team at VU Amsterdam to develop spatial models exploring how future land-use change and the energy transition shape opportunities for nature restoration. Bekijk vacature Postdoc: Climate, human behaviour and dengue forecasting 0.8 / 1 Faculty of Science Researcher / Postdoc Postdoc Sluit op 19-11-2026 Publicatiedatum 06-11-2026 0.0 km Do you want to understand how climate and human responses shape disease risk? Join FEEL at Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam and help exploring whether emotions can improve dengue forecasts. Bekijk vacature Postdoc in Topological Data Analysis 0.8 / 1 Faculty of Science Researcher / Postdoc Postdoc Sluit op 06-12-2026 Publicatiedatum 05-11-2026 0.0 km Do you have an inquisitive mind and a passion for mathematics? Please apply for a Postdoctoral position at Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam. Bekijk vacature Postdoc in Geometric and Combinatorial Topology 0.8 / 1 Faculty of Science Researcher / Postdoc MSc Sluit op 06-12-2026 Publicatiedatum 28-10-2026 0.0 km Do you have an inquisitive mind and a passion for Mathematics? Please apply for a Postdoctoral position "
