    "https://werkenbij.vu.nl/vacatures/postdoctoral-researcher-leadership-ai-and-the-future-of-work-amsterdam-1361111": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher: Leadership, AI and the Future of Work",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher: Leadership, AI and the Future of Work | Werken bij VU Vacatures Faculteit/Dienst Faculteiten Academisch Centrum Tandheelkunde Amsterdam (ACTA) Faculteit der Bètawetenschappen Faculteit der Gedrags- en Bewegingswetenschappen Faculteit der  Sociale en Geesteswetenschappen Faculteit der Geneeskunde Faculteit der Rechtsgeleerdheid School of Business and Economics Diensten Bestuurszaken Communicatie & Marketing Dienst Universitaire Relaties & Fondswerving Facilitaire Campus Organisatie Financiën HRM, Arbo & Milieu Informatietechnologie Student- en Onderwijszaken Universiteitsbibliotheek Jong talent PhD Student-assistent Stage Over ons Over ons VU arbeidsvoorwaarden: uitgebreid en flexibel VU persoonlijk: ontwikkelen, erkennen en waarderen VU identiteit: veilig, verantwoord en inclusief VU Campus: groen, rookvrij en sportief VU sollicitatie: proces, screening en participatie Ik ben een kandidaat Ga naar mijn persoonlijke pagina Log in als medewerker Log in 0 NL EN Postdoctoral Researcher: Leadership, AI and the Future of Work Ga terug VU Hoofdgebouw 1 / 1 Research Sluit op 05-01-2027 Amsterdam School of Business and Economics Postdoc Publicatiedatum 20-11-2026 Solliciteer direct Postdoctoral Researcher: Leadership, AI and the Future of Work VU Hoofdgebouw Amsterdam 1 / 1 School of Business and Economics Research Postdoc Sluit op 05-01-2027 Publicatiedatum 20-11-2026 Solliciteer direct Do you want to help shape how leaders and employees use AI to create better work? Join our VU People@Work Research Group. Your function Across sectors, organizations are investing heavily in AI and digital technologies. Yet technological change does not automatically lead to better work, better learning, or better organizational outcomes. Whether technology augments or constrains employees often depends on how workers and leaders shape its implementation and use in everyday practice. Understanding these processes has become one of the central challenges facing organizations today. The People@Work Research Group at the Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Researcher to join the NWA-funded AUGMENT project, a large-scale collaboration between universities, research institutes, policymakers, employers, employee representatives, and technology developers. AUGMENT aims to understand how AI and other digital technologies can be implemented in ways that strengthen rather than replace human capabilities at work. The successful candidate will be embedded in Work Package 2, which examines how workers actively shape the trajectory and impact of technological change. Central to this work package is the assumption that employees are not merely recipients of new technologies, but active agents whose behaviors, decisions, and interactions influence whether technologies become beneficial for workers, organizations, and society. The position focuses on WP2.1 ( Guiding Technology Augmentation ), which investigates how leaders and employees jointly shape the successful implementation of AI and other digital technologies in organizations. Specifically, the project seeks to understand how leadership behaviors, workplace conditions, and social dynamics encourage employees to experiment with, learn from, and effectively integrate new technologies into their work. More broadly, the project aims to identify the conditions under which AI implementation promotes employee learning, innovation, and sustainable performance. To address these questions, the project combines longitudinal field research, experience sampling methods, and close collaboration with organizations that are actively implementing digital technologies. The postdoctoral researcher will play a central role in designing and conducting these studies and will have substantial opportunities to shape the scientific direction of the project and develop an independent research profile within the broader AUGMENT program. Your duties As postdoctoral researcher you will: lead the scientific activities of WP2.1, including the design, coordination, and execution of longitudinal field studies that examine how leaders and employees jointly shape the implementation and use of AI and other digital technologies in organizations; collect and analyse intensive longitudinal data (e.g., multi-wave surveys and experience sampling studies) to investigate how leadership, employee agency, and workplace conditions influence technology implementation, learning, and innovation over time; collaborate closely with consortium partners and organizations implementing AI and digital technologies; publish findings in leading international journals and present research at international conferences; contribute to the development of practical tools, guidelines, and recommendations that support worker-augmenting technology implementation; actively participate in consortium-wide meetings, workshops, stakeholder engagement activities, and other collaborative initiatives within AUGMENT; contribute a limited amount of teaching (approximately 0.10-0.15 FTE; e.g., tutorial teaching at the Bachelor's and Master's level, and occasional guest lectures); contribute to a collaborative, inclusive, and supportive research environment within the People@Work Research Group, the department, and the wider AUGMENT consortium. The wider AUGMENT consortium connects research on changing work, worker agency, technology design and implementation. Thus, this postdoc position offers ample opportunities to work across disciplines, collaborate actively with organizations and researchers from different institutes, and translate research into meaningful guidance and tools for practice. Your profile We are looking for an ambitious and collaborative researcher with a strong interest in the human side of technological change. You have: a PhD in Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Work and Organizational Psychology, Organizational Studies, or a related social science discipline, completed prior to the start of the postdoc. a strong interest in leadership, employee proactivity, workplace learning, technology implementation, organizational change, and/or future of work. demonstrated expertise in designing and conducting quantitative research, including longitudinal field studies, multi-wave surveys, experience sample methods, diary studies, field experiments, or related approaches advanced quantitative and statistical analysis skills. strong project management skills and the ability to independently coordinate complex research activities involving multiple stakeholders. a proven publication track record, including publications or advanced-stage manuscripts (revise & resubmit or under review) in well-regarded peer-reviewed journals in organizational behavior, organization, and management studies. familiarity with the academic publication process and the ability to disseminate research to both scholarly and broader audiences. experience with, or enthusiasm for, collaborating with organizations and collecting data i real-world organizational settings. a proactive, self-starting attitude and the ability to independently develop and advance research projects. a collaborative, collegial, and professional mindset, with a willingness to contribute to a supportive research environment. excellent academic writing and speaking skills in English. excellent command of written and spoken Dutch (B2 level and up) is a preference, but not a requirement. What do we offer? A challenging position in a socially engaged organisation. At VU Amsterdam, you contribute to education, research and service for a better world. And that is valuable. So in return for your efforts, we offer you: a salary of minimum € 3.706,00 (Scale 10) and maximum € 5.760,00 (Scale 10) gross per month, on a full-time basis. This is based on UFO profile Researcher 4. The exact salary depends on your education and experience. a position for 1 FTE. Your employment contract will initially last 1 year. Afterwards, the appointment may be extended for an additional 1 year based on satisfactory performance. the preferred starting date is May 2026. We also offer you attractive fringe benefits and regulations. Some examples: A full-time 38-hour working week comes with a holiday leave entitlement of 232 hours per year. If you choose to work 40 hours, you have 96 extra holiday leave hours on an annual basis. For part-timers, this is calculated pro rata. 8% holiday allowance and 8.3% end-of-year bonus optional model for designing a personalized benefits package contribution to commuting expenses group insured for partial disability with employer contribution of 50% of the premium About us VU People @ Work group The VU People @ Work research group is a disciplinary and methodologically diverse group of experts who create knowledge for organizations to understand and proactively manage the current developments in employment practices, technology, demography, and organizational structures. Our research is anchored in three interconnected pillars: work design, work relationships, and development. Together, these pillars guide our research towards enabling individuals and teams to be happy, healthy, and productive. Our expertise spans a broad range of topics, including the future of work, careers, leadership, Diversity and Inclusion, meaningful work, well-being, proactivity, HRM, sustainability, learning community, and innovation . School of Business and Economics We at the School of Business and Economics (SBE) at VU Amsterdam bring together socially relevant teaching and research in the areas of business administration and economics. We focus on real-life issues that have a huge impact on society, economics and ecology: from robotics to big data, and from job market participation to change management. Collaboration and cooperation, transparency and social responsibility are four keywords that embody our approach. Students, researchers and staff at SBE share real-world knowledge in order to devise solutions together to global economic and social challenges. In order to make a positive impact on the world, society and the lives of others. Are you interested in joining SBE? You will work in a stimulating, dynamic and international environment with motivated colleagues dedicated to helping society make informed choices. SBE employs roughly 600 staff, with 7,250 students enrolled in the Bachelor’s and Master’s programmes and 1,700 executive students. Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam stands for values-driven education and research. We are open-minded experts with the ability to think freely - a broader mind. Maintaining an entrepreneurial perspective and concentrating on diversity, significance and humanity, we work on sustainable solutions with social impact. By joining forces, across the boundaries of disciplines, we work towards a better world for people and planet. Together we create a safe and respectful working and study climate, and an inspiring environment for education and research. Learn more about our codes of conduct We are located on one physical campus, in the heart of Amsterdam's Zuidas business district, with excellent location and accessibility. Over 6,150 staff work at the VU and over 31,000 students attend academic education. Diversity Diversity is the driving force of VU Amsterdam. VU wants to be accessible and receptive to diversity in disciplines, cultures, ideas, nationalities, beliefs, preferences and worldviews. We believe that trust, respect, interest and differences lead to new insights and innovation, to sharpness and clarity, to excellence and a broader understanding. We stand for an inclusive community and believe that diversity and internationalization contribute to the quality of education, research and our services. Therefore, we are always searching for people whose backgrounds and experience contribute to the diversity of the VU community. Interested Are you interested in this position and do you believe that your experience will contribute to the further development of our university? In that case, we encourage you to submit your application, including: Cover letter in which you describe your motivation for the position and how your expertise aligns with this A CV (with the list of current publications, papers in review, and working papers), Research statement outlining your research interest and explaining how your expertise contributes to the study of leadership, employee agency, workplace learning, technology implementation, and/or the future of work; Up to two publications or manuscripts in progress, One academic letter of recommendation and the contact information of one additional academic reference. Submitting a diploma and a knowledge security check are part of the application procedure. Applications received by e-mail will not be considered. Acquisition in response to this advertisement is not appreciated. Your function Across sectors, organizations are investing heavily in AI and digital technologies. Yet technological change does not automatically lead to better work, better learning, or better organizational outcomes. Whether technology augments or constrains employees often depends on how workers and leaders shape its implementation and use in everyday practice. Understanding these processes has become one of the central challenges facing organizations today. The People@Work Research Group at the Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Researcher to join the NWA-funded AUGMENT project, a large-scale collaboration between universities, research institutes, policymakers, employers, employee representatives, and technology developers. AUGMENT aims to understand how AI and other digital technologies can be implemented in ways that strengthen rather than replace human capabilities at work. The successful candidate will be embedded in Work Package 2, which examines how workers actively shape the trajectory and impact of technological change. Central to this work package is the assumption that employees are not merely recipients of new technologies, but active agents whose behaviors, decisions, and interactions influence whether technologies become beneficial for workers, organizations, and society. The position focuses on WP2.1 ( Guiding Technology Augmentation ), which investigates how leaders and employees jointly shape the successful implementation of AI and other digital technologies in organizations. Specifically, the project seeks to understand how leadership behaviors, workplace conditions, and social dynamics encourage employees to experiment with, learn from, and effectively integrate new technologies into their work. More broadly, the project aims to identify the conditions under which AI implementation promotes employee learning, innovation, and sustainable performance. To address these questions, the project combines longitudinal field research, experience sampling methods, and close collaboration with organizations that are actively implementing digital technologies. The postdoctoral researcher will play a central role in designing and conducting these studies and will have substantial opportunities to shape the scientific direction of the project and develop an independent research profile within the broader AUGMENT program. Your duties As postdoctoral researcher you will: lead the scientific activities of WP2.1, including the design, coordination, and execution of longitudinal field studies that examine how leaders and employees jointly shape the implementation and use of AI and other digital technologies in organizations; collect and analyse intensive longitudinal data (e.g., multi-wave surveys and experience sampling studies) to investigate how leadership, employee agency, and workplace conditions influence technology implementation, learning, and innovation over time; collaborate closely with consortium partners and organizations implementing AI and digital technologies; publish findings in leading international journals and present research at international conferences; contribute to the development of practical tools, guidelines, and recommendations that support worker-augmenting technology implementation; actively participate in consortium-wide meetings, workshops, stakeholder engagement activities, and other collaborative initiatives within AUGMENT; contribute a limited amount of teaching (approximately 0.10-0.15 FTE; e.g., tutorial teaching at the Bachelor's and Master's level, and occasional guest lectures); contribute to a collaborative, inclusive, and supportive research environment within the People@Work Research Group, the department, and the wider AUGMENT consortium. The wider AUGMENT consortium connects research on changing work, worker agency, technology design and implementation. Thus, this postdoc position offers ample opportunities to work across disciplines, collaborate actively with organizations and researchers from different institutes, and translate research into meaningful guidance and tools for practice. Your profile We are looking for an ambitious and collaborative researcher with a strong interest in the human side of technological change. You have: a PhD in Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Work and Organizational Psychology, Organizational Studies, or a related social science discipline, completed prior to the start of the postdoc. a strong interest in leadership, employee proactivity, workplace learning, technology implementation, organizational change, and/or future of work. demonstrated expertise in designing and conducting quantitative research, including longitudinal field studies, multi-wave surveys, experience sample methods, diary studies, field experiments, or related approaches advanced quantitative and statistical analysis skills. strong project management skills and the ability to independently coordinate complex research activities involving multiple stakeholders. a proven publication track record, including publications or advanced-stage manuscripts (revise & resubmit or under review) in well-regarded peer-reviewed journals in organizational behavior, organization, and management studies. familiarity with the academic publication process and the ability to disseminate research to both scholarly and broader audiences. experience with, or enthusiasm for, collaborating with organizations and collecting data i real-world organizational settings. a proactive, self-starting attitude and the ability to independently develop and advance research projects. a collaborative, collegial, and professional mindset, with a willingness to contribute to a supportive research environment. excellent academic writing and speaking skills in English. excellent command of written and spoken Dutch (B2 level and up) is a preference, but not a requirement. What do we offer? A challenging position in a socially engaged organisation. At VU Amsterdam, you contribute to education, research and service for a better world. And that is valuable. So in return for your efforts, we offer you: a salary of minimum € 3.706,00 (Scale 10) and maximum € 5.760,00 (Scale 10) gross per month, on a full-time basis. This is based on UFO profile Researcher 4. The exact salary depends on your education and experience. a position for 1 FTE. Your employment contract will initially last 1 year. Afterwards, the appointment may be extended for an additional 1 year based on satisfactory performance. the preferred starting date is May 2026. We also offer you attractive fringe benefits and regulations. Some examples: A full-time 38-hour working week comes with a holiday leave entitlement of 232 hours per year. If you choose to work 40 hours, you have 96 extra holiday leave hours on an annual basis. For part-timers, this is calculated pro rata. 8% holiday allowance and 8.3% end-of-year bonus optional model for designing a personalized benefits package "
