    "https://werkenbij.vu.nl/vacatures/phd-ai-for-early-detection-of-cardiometabolic-diseases-using-oral-health-data-amsterdam-1359175": {
      "title": "PhD: AI for early detection of cardiometabolic diseases using oral health data",
      "description": "PhD: AI for early detection of cardiometabolic diseases using oral health data | Werken bij VU Vacatures Faculteit/Dienst Faculteiten Academisch Centrum Tandheelkunde Amsterdam (ACTA) Faculteit der Bètawetenschappen Faculteit der Gedrags- en Bewegingswetenschappen Faculteit der  Sociale en Geesteswetenschappen Faculteit der Geneeskunde Faculteit der Rechtsgeleerdheid School of Business and Economics Diensten Bestuurszaken Communicatie & Marketing Dienst Universitaire Relaties & Fondswerving Facilitaire Campus Organisatie Financiën HRM, Arbo & Milieu Informatietechnologie Student- en Onderwijszaken Universiteitsbibliotheek Jong talent PhD Student-assistent Stage Over ons Over ons VU arbeidsvoorwaarden: uitgebreid en flexibel VU persoonlijk: ontwikkelen, erkennen en waarderen VU identiteit: veilig, verantwoord en inclusief VU Campus: groen, rookvrij en sportief VU sollicitatie: proces, screening en participatie Ik ben een kandidaat Ga naar mijn persoonlijke pagina Log in als medewerker Log in 0 NL EN PhD: AI for early detection of cardiometabolic diseases using oral health data Ga terug ACTA Gebouw 1 / 1 PhD Sluit op 01-03-2027 Amsterdam Academisch Centrum Tandheelkunde Amsterdam MSc Publicatiedatum 16-11-2026 Solliciteer direct PhD: AI for early detection of cardiometabolic diseases using oral health data ACTA Gebouw Amsterdam 1 / 1 Academisch Centrum Tandheelkunde Amsterdam PhD MSc Sluit op 01-03-2027 Publicatiedatum 16-11-2026 Solliciteer direct Are you excited about multimodal and generative AI, healthcare innovation, and translating advanced data science into real-world clinical impact? Then apply for this PhD position. Your function You develop and clinically validate innovative AI-based screening models integrating retrospective and prospective data from multiple sources. These models are applied in the context of oral and systemic health, with a particular focus on the early detection of cardiometabolic diseases (CMD). You also assess the usability of the models in clinical practice. Working within a multidisciplinary research team, you help translate advanced AI methods into clinically relevant applications. In addition to your research activities, you may contribute to ongoing educational activities within the department, including the supervision of bachelor's and master's theses. About the project Cardiovascular diseases, diabetes, oral cancer and osteoporosis remain among the most important public health challenges in Europe. Increasing evidence suggests that oral health and general health are closely connected, yet these links are not routinely used to support disease prevention and early detection. The MYDIAG.AI project, funded by EU-Horizon, aims to address this gap by developing a generative AI-powered virtual assistant capable of analyzing multiple sources of health information, including electronic health records, clinical notes, intraoral photographs, and panoramic dental X-rays. The AI assistant will help healthcare professionals identify potential health risks, support clinical decision-making, and generate draft medical notes and referral letters. By bringing together expertise in dentistry, medicine, data science and AI, MYDIAG.AI seeks to strengthen collaboration between oral healthcare and general healthcare. The Academic Center for Dentistry Amsterdam (ACTA) will focus on the development and validation of a multimodal AI-model, which will serve as a core component of the virtual assistant. ACTA will also contribute to the clinical validation and implementation of the virtual assistant in dental settings. Both retrospective and prospective observational data will be collected and used in the study. Your profile A MSc in (Medical) Informatics, Technical Medicine, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Computer Science, or a closely related discipline, preferably with experience in health and biomedical applications Experience with the development, validation, implementation, and evaluation of AI models (preferably in healthcare or biomedical research), including machine learning, deep learning, generative AI (e.g. LLMs and VLMs), and multimodal AI approaches integrating structured and unstructured data Proficiency in Python, R, or similar data science environments Ability to communicate complex technical concepts to both healthcare professionals and AI/data science specialists, bridging the gap between disciplines and contributing effectively to multidisciplinary research collaboration Excellent written and spoken English Strong analytical and organizational skills Affinity with teaching and the supervision of bachelor's and master's students The following qualifications are considered an advantage: A background in dentistry, oral health sciences, dental hygiene, cardiometabolic health, or a related field, and/or experience in oral-systemic health, dental epidemiology, or dental public health Experience working with large-scale healthcare data, including electronic health records (EHRs), healthcare databases, and linked registry datasets Evidence of scientific writing skills through publications and/or conference presentations What do we offer? A salary ranging from €3,204 gross per month in the first year to €4,051 gross per month in the fourth year, based on a full-time appointment (38 hours per week) and in accordance with the UFO profile PhD candidate. A 4-year full-time PhD position (initial 1-year contract, extended by 3 years following positive evaluation) In addition, we offer an attractive package of employee benefits and arrangements. Examples include: A full-time 38-hour working week with 232 hours of annual leave An additional 96 hours of annual leave when working 40 hours per week 8% holiday allowance and 8.3% end-of-year bonus Solid pension scheme (ABP) Collective disability insurance, with the employer contributing 50% of the premium Commuting allowance About us ACTA is the joint Faculty of Dentistry of the University of Amsterdam and Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam and is internationally recognized for its research, education, and patient care in oral health. Interested Do you recognize yourself in this profile and are you excited about contributing to this research project? We look forward to receiving your application. Please upload: A detailed CV A cover letter describing your background, motivation and skills (max. 1 page) Transcripts with all your grades from your BSc and MSc studies Your MSc thesis, or a draft if it is not finished yet Your diploma(s) The names and contact details of two academic references Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis and candidates are therefore encouraged to apply early. The initial selection for first-round interviews will take place on Friday, 15 January 2027. First-round interviews will take place either on Tuesday, 26 January 2027 (morning) or Friday, 29 January 2027. Candidates shortlisted for a second-round interview will be invited to attend on Friday, 5 February 2027. Applicants are kindly requested to keep all interview dates available. Applications will remain open until the position is filled. The preferred start date for the successful candidate is 1 March 2027. For questions about this position, please contact Dr. Naichuan Su (e-mail [email protected] ) Applications received by e-mail will not be considered. Acquisition in response to this advertisement is not appreciated. Your function You develop and clinically validate innovative AI-based screening models integrating retrospective and prospective data from multiple sources. These models are applied in the context of oral and systemic health, with a particular focus on the early detection of cardiometabolic diseases (CMD). You also assess the usability of the models in clinical practice. Working within a multidisciplinary research team, you help translate advanced AI methods into clinically relevant applications. In addition to your research activities, you may contribute to ongoing educational activities within the department, including the supervision of bachelor's and master's theses. About the project Cardiovascular diseases, diabetes, oral cancer and osteoporosis remain among the most important public health challenges in Europe. Increasing evidence suggests that oral health and general health are closely connected, yet these links are not routinely used to support disease prevention and early detection. The MYDIAG.AI project, funded by EU-Horizon, aims to address this gap by developing a generative AI-powered virtual assistant capable of analyzing multiple sources of health information, including electronic health records, clinical notes, intraoral photographs, and panoramic dental X-rays. The AI assistant will help healthcare professionals identify potential health risks, support clinical decision-making, and generate draft medical notes and referral letters. By bringing together expertise in dentistry, medicine, data science and AI, MYDIAG.AI seeks to strengthen collaboration between oral healthcare and general healthcare. The Academic Center for Dentistry Amsterdam (ACTA) will focus on the development and validation of a multimodal AI-model, which will serve as a core component of the virtual assistant. ACTA will also contribute to the clinical validation and implementation of the virtual assistant in dental settings. Both retrospective and prospective observational data will be collected and used in the study. Your profile A MSc in (Medical) Informatics, Technical Medicine, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Computer Science, or a closely related discipline, preferably with experience in health and biomedical applications Experience with the development, validation, implementation, and evaluation of AI models (preferably in healthcare or biomedical research), including machine learning, deep learning, generative AI (e.g. LLMs and VLMs), and multimodal AI approaches integrating structured and unstructured data Proficiency in Python, R, or similar data science environments Ability to communicate complex technical concepts to both healthcare professionals and AI/data science specialists, bridging the gap between disciplines and contributing effectively to multidisciplinary research collaboration Excellent written and spoken English Strong analytical and organizational skills Affinity with teaching and the supervision of bachelor's and master's students The following qualifications are considered an advantage: A background in dentistry, oral health sciences, dental hygiene, cardiometabolic health, or a related field, and/or experience in oral-systemic health, dental epidemiology, or dental public health Experience working with large-scale healthcare data, including electronic health records (EHRs), healthcare databases, and linked registry datasets Evidence of scientific writing skills through publications and/or conference presentations What do we offer? A salary ranging from €3,204 gross per month in the first year to €4,051 gross per month in the fourth year, based on a full-time appointment (38 hours per week) and in accordance with the UFO profile PhD candidate. A 4-year full-time PhD position (initial 1-year contract, extended by 3 years following positive evaluation) In addition, we offer an attractive package of employee benefits and arrangements. Examples include: A full-time 38-hour working week with 232 hours of annual leave An additional 96 hours of annual leave when working 40 hours per week 8% holiday allowance and 8.3% end-of-year bonus Solid pension scheme (ABP) Collective disability insurance, with the employer contributing 50% of the premium Commuting allowance About us ACTA is the joint Faculty of Dentistry of the University of Amsterdam and Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam and is internationally recognized for its research, education, and patient care in oral health. Vragen over de vacature? Neem contact op met Naichuan Su Universitair docent Stuur een e-mail Interested Do you recognize yourself in this profile and are you excited about contributing to this research project? We look forward to receiving your application. Please upload: A detailed CV A cover letter describing your background, motivation and skills (max. 1 page) Transcripts with all your grades from your BSc and MSc studies Your MSc thesis, or a draft if it is not finished yet Your diploma(s) The names and contact details of two academic references Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis and candidates are therefore encouraged to apply early. The initial selection for first-round interviews will take place on Friday, 15 January 2027. First-round interviews will take place either on Tuesday, 26 January 2027 (morning) or Friday, 29 January 2027. Candidates shortlisted for a second-round interview will be invited to attend on Friday, 5 February 2027. Applicants are kindly requested to keep all interview dates available. Applications will remain open until the position is filled. The preferred start date for the successful candidate is 1 March 2027. For questions about this position, please contact Dr. Naichuan Su (e-mail [email protected] ) Applications received by e-mail will not be considered. Acquisition in response to this advertisement is not appreciated. Vragen over de vacature? Neem contact op met Naichuan Su Universitair docent Stuur een e-mail Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1 Sollicitatie ontvangen Wij hebben je sollicitatie goed ontvangen. We streven ernaar om je zo snel mogelijk een eerste reactie te geven. Normaal gesproken is dat twee weken na het verstrijken van de deadline. Stap 2 Screening CV Een selectiecommissie beoordeelt of je voldoet aan de gestelde wensen/eisen voor de vacature. Bij een positieve beoordeling nodigen we je uit voor een eerste (hybride) sollicitatiegesprek. Stap 3 1e Gesprek Sollicitatiegesprekken vinden veelal plaats op een VU- locatie, maar soms word je eerst uitgenodigd voor een videogesprek. De VU maakt hiervoor gebruik van MS teams. Stap 4 2e Gesprek Voor het tweede gesprek vragen we je meestal om naar onze VU campus te komen. Stap 5 Pre-employment screening Het overleggen van een diploma wordt altijd gevraagd bij indiensttreding. Afhankelijk van de functie kan een assessment onderdeel uitmaken van de sollicitatieprocedure. Stap 6 Optioneel antecedentenonderzoek Afhankelijk van de functie en het bijbehorende risicoprofiel, kan een antecedentenonderzoek door de VU worden uitgevoerd. Daarbij kan worden gevraagd om referenties en/of een Verklaring omtrent Gedrag (VOG) aan te leveren. In het kader van kennisveiligheid kunnen wij ook publieke beschikbare social media accounts en publieke uitlatingen van jou op internet bekijken. Stap 7 In dienst Welkom je bent in dienst bij de Vrije Universiteit!! Andere interessante vacatures PhD position Societal entrepreneurship in equitable global health innovation 0.8 / 1 Faculty of Science PhD MSc Sluit op 03-12-2026 Publicatiedatum 17-11-2026 0.4 km Would you like to study how organisations in global health innovation balance competing expectations and responsibilities, together with industry, civil society, funders and regulators? Then you should apply! Bekijk vacature PhD in Labour Migration in Digital Industrial Policy 1 / 1 Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities PhD MSc Sluit op 01-12-2026 Publicatiedatum 05-11-2026 0.4 km How is the EU’s quest for digital autonomy reshaping labour markets? Join this PhD project to explore how policymakers, employers and trade unions shape labour migration in Europe’s digital transformation. Bekijk vacature PhD in Early Modern Religious Debates. The use of AI in analysing sources 1 / 1 Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities PhD MSc Sluit op 27-11-2026 Publicatiedatum 28-10-2026 0.4 km Do you want to explore original historical documents, examine religious debates of the early modern period, and discover the potential of AI in analysing ancient sources? Then apply to this PhD position! Bekijk vacature PhD Position Early Modern Religious Debates and the Public Sphere 1 / 1 Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities PhD MSc Sluit op 27-11-2026 Publicatiedatum 28-10-2026 0.4 km Do you want to explore original historical documents, examine religious debates of the early modern period, and detect the roots of the current notion of a public sphere? Then apply to this PhD position! Bekijk vacature PhD in experimental physics: how do you make the first antimatter molecule? 0.8 / 1 Faculty of Science PhD MSc Sluit op 28-02-2027 Publicatiedatum 23-10-2026 0.4 km Help make the first measurement of how a proton and a hydrogen atom bind into a molecule. With extreme-UV lasers and ion traps, you will study the most fundamental atomic collisions and find out how the first antimatter molecules could be made. Bekijk vacature PhD Position in Space Law and Artificial Intelligence 0.8 / 1 Faculty of Law PhD LL.M Sluit op 27-11-2026 Publicatiedatum 07-10-2026 0.4 km Who sets the rules when AI turns Earth Observation data into decisions about security, resilience and society? Join us as a PhD researcher and help shape the unique intersection of space law and artificial intelligence. Bekijk vacature Mis jouw droombaan niet! Stel job alert in Privacy Cookies Disclaimer VU.nl Deze website maakt gebruik van cookies Wij, en derde partijen, maken op onze website gebruik van cookies. Wij gebruiken cookies om ervoor te zorgen dat onze website goed functioneert, om jouw voorkeuren op te slaan, om inzicht te verkrijgen in bezoekersgedrag, maar ook voor marketing en social media doeleinden (laten zien van gepersonaliseerde advertenties). Door op ‘Accepteren’ te klikken, ga je akkoord met het gebruik van alle cookies. In onze Cookieverklaring kun je meer lezen over de cookies die wij gebruiken en kun je jouw voorkeuren opslaan of wijzigen.  Door ‘Weigeren’ te klikken ga je alleen akkoord met het gebruik van functionele cookies. Functioneel Functionele cookies zorgen ervoor dat deze website informatie kan onthouden die van invloed is op het gedrag en de vormgeving van de website, zoals bijvoorbeeld welke vacatures jouw favorieten zijn. Statistieken Statistische cookies helpen ons te begrijpen hoe bezoekers deze website gebruiken, door anoniem gegevens te verzamelen en te rapporteren. Marketing Marketing cookies worden op deze site gebruikt om eventueel video’s via YouTube af te kunnen spelen. Verder ook om relevante advertenties weer te geven tijdens het bezoeken van andere websites. Zelf instellen Weigeren Accepteer geselecteerde cookies Accepteren Lees meer in de cookieverklaring"
